# sow.rish — sow the public seed from the standing field.
#
# Reads template-manifest.bron and writes the identity-clean template subset
# into seed/ (gitignored; the fresh Option-B public repo that becomes
# grain-os/grain). personal and sub_exclude paths never enter; name-bearing
# files are withheld for the M3 scrub pass, so the seed is clean by
# construction. The heavy file work is a POSIX seam in
# tools/fixtures/sow_project.sh; this script is the thin Rishi driver.
#
# Plans: external-research/20260808-045124 (Movement I, the mechanism) and
# 20260808-183336 (the compact root). Layout: 20260808-183636 (field + seed).
# Safety is proven separately by tools/s/sow_witness.rish.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/s/sow.rish

let proj = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/sow_project.sh"]
say proj.out
assert proj.ok else "sow projection failed to run"
assert (proj.out contains "SOW_OK") else "sow projection did not complete cleanly"
say "sow: seed/ projected — run tools/s/sow_witness.rish to prove it clean"
